        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westerville%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When a railroad was built farther south of Westerville in 1886, the town gradually declined.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westerville%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Westerville post office opened in 1882 and became a hub for local communication.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westerville%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "County fairs were held in Westerville in 1883 and 1884, showcasing local agriculture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westerville%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
